# Deliberately empty.
#
# `pnpm check:boot` passes this to `wrangler dev --env-file`, which stops
# wrangler loading `.dev.vars` / `.env` / `.env.local` from the target app.
# `BOOT_VARS` in src/lib/boot-check.ts is then the Worker's whole env, by
# construction rather than by an allowlist somebody has to maintain.
#
# Adding a key here would defeat the point: the check proves the built bundle
# runs, and must behave identically on a developer's machine and in CI. If a
# Worker needs another variable to serve a request, add it to `BOOT_VARS`, where
# it is visible, typed and asserted against the real env schema.
#
# The name must not start with `.env` — `.gitignore` excludes that, and an
# ignored fixture would exist locally and be missing in CI.
